PDCS -- COIN-OR submission package 20261001-r2
===========================================

PDCS is a Julia primal-dual solver for large-scale conic optimization with CPU
and optional CUDA GPU implementations. Supported test cases cover second-order,
exponential and dual exponential cones.

Project home: https://github.com/ZikaiXiong/PDCS
Submission source: https://github.com/zhenweilin/PDCS_fork/tree/coin_or
Base source commit: 966385736b25bea85f29be81bff8984f35c3b7af
Author metadata updated to include all four paper authors; solver code unchanged.
Project manager: Zikai Xiong <zikai.xiong@northwestern.edu>
Authors: Zhenwei Lin, Zikai Xiong, Dongdong Ge, and Yinyu Ye (AUTHORS).
License: Apache-2.0; see LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.
Support / bugs / features: https://github.com/ZikaiXiong/PDCS/issues
Code of conduct: https://www.coin-or.org/code-of-conduct/

Quick start
-----------
Install Julia 1.10 or newer, then run from this folder:

    bash build.sh

This installs declared Julia dependencies, runs the SOC example and the default
CPU test suite. Set JULIA=/path/to/julia if Julia is not on PATH. Initial package
installation needs Internet access; no research dataset is required.
INSTALL and README.md retain the original package instructions.

For GPU checks, use an allocated NVIDIA GPU and a compatible CUDA toolkit:

    MODE=gpu CUDA_HOME=/path/to/cuda GPU_ARCH=sm_80 bash build.sh

Use sm_90 for H100. MODE=all runs both CPU and GPU checks. The wrapper selects
the tested CUDA.jl 5.11.3 by default; CUDA_VERSION overrides it. Native libraries
are built from the included source. The wrapper removes LD_LIBRARY_PATH only
from Julia processes, following the documented Quest configuration.
Exit 0 means the requested checks passed; any failed assertion exits nonzero.
GPU mode fails when hardware is unavailable. It does not silently skip tests.
No linear-programming or rotated-SOC solver tests are included.

Package contents
----------------
src/, ext/, test/, examples/: solver, extension, deterministic tests and example.
Project.toml, INSTALL, CONTRIBUTING.md: dependencies and testing instructions.
AUTHORS, CITATION.txt, LICENSE, LICENSES/, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, OWNERSHIP.txt:
authorship, citations, license notices and the ownership-document status.
SOURCE_PROVENANCE.json, SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256, CHANGES_FOR_COIN_OR.txt:
source revision, checksums and preparation changes.
VALIDATION.md, validation/: actual results, environments and supporting logs.
submission/: unsigned official form templates, completion notes and cover draft.

The source is self-contained with respect to PDCS code and test data. Julia
packages and the CUDA toolchain are external dependencies, not bundled binaries.
Signed private forms, Git history, research datasets, package caches and compiled
artifacts are not part of this release folder. See submission/README.txt for the
existing signed-document record. No submission email has been sent by this task.

Verify the package before creating build artifacts:

    sha256sum -c SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256

The release label follows the companion package's 20261001-r2 naming. Actual
validation timestamps and environments are recorded separately; this package
does not claim COIN-OR acceptance or results from the cuPDLP-C example.
